From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:59:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] uts/idmap: find the rpcgen-generated header by path

NetBSD's `rpcgen` emits a bare `#include "idmap_prot.h"` where Sun's writes the
full path, so `misc/idmap` did not compile at all when built with the former.
Add `$(UTSBASE)/common/rpcsvc` to `INC_PATH` so the generated header is found
either way.

This is the same class as the `rpcb_prot.x` kernel-arm typedefs: a place where
the tree quietly assumes Sun's rpcgen. Harmless with Sun's, since the full path
still resolves.

`misc/idmap` matters because `drv/zfs` links `-N misc/idmap`.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile b/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
index c730edbba0..b843f58d65 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
+++ b/usr/src/uts/intel/idmap/Makefile
@@ -51,6 +51,15 @@ include $(UTSBASE)/intel/Makefile.intel
 #
 LDFLAGS += -Nsys/doorfs -Nstrmod/rpcmod
 
+#
+#	idmap_xdr.c is generated by rpcgen from uts/common/rpcsvc/idmap_prot.x,
+#	and rpcgen emits a bare `#include "idmap_prot.h"` -- the basename of its
+#	input, with no directory. The header is generated next to the .x file,
+#	not next to the .c, so a quoted include cannot find it from
+#	uts/common/idmap. Name the directory it does live in.
+#
+INC_PATH	+= -I$(UTSBASE)/common/rpcsvc
+
 # Function variables unused for rpcgen-generated code
 # Constant conditions for do { } while (0) macros
 #
